{
	"_comment": "Request transcripts of the prediction debounce and rate floor, replayed through _shared/lua/llm/request_plan/debounce.lua by the macOS and Linux runners. A vector names a driver_options set (or gives one), the floor of each backend in milliseconds (the floor port answers from this map and raises for a backend it lacks), and an ordered list of steps. A step calls one method of the plan with args (plus now_ms for on_dispatch and on_sent, the caller's monotonic clock in milliseconds) and lists the decisions it returns, in order, as expect, or a substring the raised message must contain as expect_error. Tokens count from 1 per plan, one per arm. An arm decision means: cancel nothing else and start a one-shot timer of delay_ms; cancel means stop that token; fire and stale answer on_timer; send and defer answer on_dispatch. driver_options is the deliberate per-driver difference: each driver asserts that its own policy equals its entry, so a drift is a red test, not a silent change. A port in another language replays this file unchanged.",
	"driver_options": {
		"macos": {
			"allow_never": true,
			"floor_scope": "global",
			"live_instant_word_end": true
		},
		"linux": {
			"allow_never": true,
			"floor_scope": "per_backend",
			"live_instant_word_end": true
		}
	},
	"vectors": [
